From 32fbec6b40418aaf5d5c3d77788f893fd9f8a4d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 13:24:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0118 -- PC-speaker square-wave SFX on the AdLib
 path (shared PIT ch0)

Campaign 2 Phase 2 (SDL side). Extends the SDL/0110 AdLib OPL music pump so a
no-SB AdLib box (real AdLib / OPL-only card, or a PicoGUS in /mode adlib) also
gets Cave Story sound effects via the motherboard PC speaker. A pure OPL card
has no DAC/DMA, so the PC speaker is the only sound-effect out it has.

Why DOS needs this: the shipped AdLib path (SDL/0110 + engine MidiBackendOpl2)
is SFX-silent by hardware -- it drives OPL2 music only. The one PCM-out an
OPL-only box has is the PC speaker. The parked PWM-DAC experiment (SDL/0111 on
feat/adlib-opl2, never merged) fed the speaker per-sample and rendered clean
tones as static on a filterless speaker. This patch instead programs PIT ch2 in
MODE 3 -- the 8253's hardware square-wave generator: the chip synthesizes the
tone itself, and the existing ~120 Hz ch0 music-pump ISR merely counts each
note's duration down and gates the speaker off when it elapses. No per-sample
feed, no second timer. ch2 does NOT touch BIOS timekeeping (ch0 does), so it is
clock-safe alongside the music pump; it reuses ONLY the ch2/0x61 acquire +
restore-on-exit discipline of the parked PWM patch, not its sample loop.

Mechanism (extends the SDL/0110 pump; DEFAULT ON on the AdLib path):
- Killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PCSPK_SFX resolved at pump Start via a strict-"0"
  test (only the literal env "0" disables; unset / anything else = ON). Since
  pump Start only runs on the no-SB AdLib path, this is inherently AdLib-scoped
  -- the repo's idiomatic "production lever default-ON with a killswitch"
  pattern. When off, the unchanged SDL/0110 music-only OplPitISR is installed:
  byte-identical to shipped v1.5.0, no ch2/0x61 touch.
- Engine-facing API (include/SDL3/SDL_dosopltimer.h; nx-engine maps Pixtone SFX
  IDs to (freq,duration) square-wave descriptors and calls it at the SFX
  trigger point): void SDL_DOSPcSpkBeep(Uint16 freq_hz, Uint16 duration_ms,
  int flush) + bool SDL_DOSPcSpkSfxEnabled(void). freq_hz==0 is a timed REST
  (for the gap in a two-note SFX); flush=1 PREEMPTS (clear queue + sounding
  note, start now), flush=0 APPENDS to a depth-4 note ring (plays after the
  current note) -- monophonic speaker sequencing for two-note SFX (pickup,
  up-chirp).
- A PC-speaker-capable ISR (OplPitBeepISR) is installed INSTEAD of OplPitISR
  only when the killswitch is on: identical clock advance + music tick + BIOS-
  INT8 chain, plus a note-duration countdown that pops the next queued note (or
  silences the speaker) on expiry. The ISR does ZERO divide -- SDL_DOSPcSpkBeep
  precomputes the ch2 divisor + duration-in-fires on the engine thread and
  stores them in the ring. Ring mutation + note start are wrapped in
  DOS_DisableInterrupts on the engine thread (single-producer vs the IRQ-0
  consumer); the ISR + ring + BeepStartNote helper are DPMI-locked at Start.
- Restore on exit (extends SDL/0110 Stop, which is also the engine's atexit
  teardown): silence the speaker + restore ch2 (benign mode 3) + port 0x61 to
  its pre-pump value, in addition to the ch0-divisor restore + IRQ-0 unhook. A
  left-on square wave is a stuck tone -- the same quit-path hazard class as the
  PIT ch0 restore.

Boot banner "audio: SDL/0118 [pcspk] square-wave SFX ..." (emits on the AdLib
path only, at pump Start) for the smoke gate.

SB-present path is unchanged: the pump is never started when an SB is hot
(SDL/0110 refuses), so SDL_DOSPcSpkBeep no-ops (guarded on pump-active) and ch2
is never touched on any SB / OPL3 / WB / GUS config.

g2k-validation items ([[dosbox_not_proxy]], DOSBox-X cannot validate real IRQ-0
timing or the analog speaker): (1) SFX audibly square-wave + music coexists on
the AdLib path; (2) clean-quit restore -- PIT ch0 back to 18.2065 Hz, ch2/0x61
restored, DOS TIME correct, no stuck tone; (3) killswitch=0 = music-only,
byte-identical to v1.5.0.

Workspace-local patch; not upstreamed (sdl_ai_policy).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 include/SDL3/SDL_dosopltimer.h     |  59 +++++++
 src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c | 259 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 311 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosopltimer.h b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosopltimer.h
index fc1d35863..3f516035e 100644
--- a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosopltimer.h
+++ b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosopltimer.h
@@ -100,6 +100,65 @@ extern SDL_DECLSPEC void SDLCALL SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpStop(void);
  */
 extern SDL_DECLSPEC bool SDLCALL SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpActive(void);
 
+/*
+ * DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0118, Campaign 2 Phase 2): PC-speaker square-wave SFX.
+ *
+ * On the no-SB AdLib path the shared PIT ch0 pump (above) also gates the
+ * motherboard PC speaker as a monophonic square-wave SFX source: a pure OPL
+ * card has no DAC/DMA, so the PC speaker is the only sound-effect out it has.
+ * Unlike the PARKED PWM-DAC experiment (which fed the speaker per-sample and
+ * rendered clean tones as static on a filterless speaker), this uses PIT ch2
+ * in MODE 3 (the 8253's hardware square-wave generator): the chip synthesizes
+ * the tone itself, and the ~120 Hz ch0 pump ISR merely counts the note's
+ * duration down and gates the speaker off when it elapses -- no per-sample
+ * feed, no second timer, and ch2 does not touch BIOS timekeeping (ch0 does).
+ *
+ * Gated by SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PCSPK_SFX: DEFAULT ON on the AdLib path, resolved
+ * at pump Start via a strict-"0" killswitch (only the literal env "0" disables;
+ * when off, the pump is music-only and byte-identical to the shipped v1.5.0
+ * AdLib path -- no ch2/0x61 touch). The engine (nx-engine) maps Pixtone SFX IDs
+ * to (freq,duration) square-wave descriptors and calls SDL_DOSPcSpkBeep below.
+ */
+
+/**
+ * Play a monophonic PC-speaker square-wave note (or a timed rest).
+ *
+ * Programs PIT ch2 (mode 3) to `freq_hz` and routes the speaker (port 0x61
+ * bits 0-1); the ch0 OPL pump ISR gates it OFF after `duration_ms`. Enqueue
+ * ONLY from the engine thread (never an ISR) -- the ring mutation is guarded
+ * internally with a brief interrupt-disable against the IRQ-0 consumer.
+ *
+ * A single PC speaker is monophonic, so two-note SFX (pickup, up-chirp) need
+ * sequencing: `flush` selects preempt-vs-queue.
+ *
+ * \param freq_hz square-wave frequency in Hz (clamped to [20,20000]); 0 == a
+ *                timed REST (speaker silent for `duration_ms`, for the gap in a
+ *                two-note sequence).
+ * \param duration_ms note length in milliseconds (clamped to [1,5000]);
+ *                    granularity is ~1 ch0 pump tick (~8 ms at 120 Hz).
+ * \param flush 1 = PREEMPT: clear the queue + any sounding note and start THIS
+ *              note immediately (a new one-shot, or the first note of a
+ *              sequence). 0 = APPEND to a small (depth-4) note ring; it plays
+ *              after the current note finishes (the later notes of a sequence).
+ *
+ * No-op unless PC-speaker SFX is enabled (SDL_DOSPcSpkSfxEnabled()) AND the ch0
+ * pump is active, so a stray call on a non-AdLib / killswitch-off build is
+ * harmless (never bangs ch2/0x61). Not a per-call hint lookup -- a cached bool.
+ *
+ * \since SDL 3 -- doskutsu workspace-local patch 0118, 2026-07-07.
+ */
+extern SDL_DECLSPEC void SDLCALL SDL_DOSPcSpkBeep(Uint16 freq_hz, Uint16 duration_ms, int flush);
+
+/**
+ * \returns true if PC-speaker square-wave SFX is ENABLED for this process
+ *          (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PCSPK_SFX != "0", resolved at pump Start on the
+ *          AdLib path). The engine gates its SFX->beep mapping on this. False
+ *          when the killswitch is "0" or the pump never started (e.g. an SB is
+ *          present, so the pump refused and the AdLib path is not in use).
+ * \since SDL 3 -- doskutsu workspace-local patch 0118, 2026-07-07.
+ */
+extern SDL_DECLSPEC bool SDLCALL SDL_DOSPcSpkSfxEnabled(void);
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
diff --git a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
index 285180bb0..29751d626 100644
--- a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
+++ b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
@@ -1264,6 +1264,67 @@ static volatile Uint64   s_now_ms = 0;        /* monotonic ms for the tick cb */
 static volatile uint32_t s_bios_accum = 0;    /* fractional toward the 18.2 Hz BIOS tick */
 static SDL_DOSMidiTickCallback s_pump_tick_cb = NULL;
 
+/* ========================================================================
+ * DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0118, Campaign 2 Phase 2): PC-speaker square-wave SFX
+ * ========================================================================
+ * Extends the SDL/0110 pump so a no-SB AdLib box also gets Cave Story SFX via
+ * the motherboard PC speaker -- but using PIT ch2 in MODE 3 (the 8253 hardware
+ * square-wave generator), NOT the parked SDL/0111 PWM-DAC (which fed the
+ * speaker per-sample and rendered clean tones as static). The chip synthesizes
+ * the tone; the ch0 pump ISR only counts each note's duration down and gates
+ * the speaker off, then advances a small note ring (for two-note SFX). ch2 does
+ * NOT touch BIOS timekeeping (ch0 does), so it is clock-safe alongside the music
+ * pump. DEFAULT ON on the AdLib path via the strict-"0" killswitch
+ * SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PCSPK_SFX (resolved at Start); when off, the unchanged
+ * SDL/0110 music-only ISR is installed (byte-identical to v1.5.0, no ch2/0x61
+ * touch). Engine-facing API contract: include/SDL3/SDL_dosopltimer.h. */
+
+#define PCSPK_NOTE_RING   4              /* queued-note ring depth (power of two) */
+#define PCSPK_NOTE_MASK   (PCSPK_NOTE_RING - 1)
+#define PCSPK_FREQ_MIN    20u
+#define PCSPK_FREQ_MAX    20000u
+#define PCSPK_DUR_MAX     5000u
+
+/* Killswitch + restore state (resolved / captured once at pump Start). */
+static bool     s_pcspk_sfx_enabled = false; /* SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PCSPK_SFX != "0" (default ON) */
+static Uint8    s_pcspk_saved_61    = 0;     /* port 0x61 saved at Start, restored at Stop */
+static uint32_t s_pcspk_fire_hz     = 0;     /* ch0 pump fire rate, for ms->tick conversion */
+
+/* Currently-sounding note (ISR-owned; engine thread only writes under cli). */
+static volatile uint32_t s_beep_ticks   = 0;    /* ch0-pump fires remaining (0 == idle) */
+static volatile bool     s_beep_playing = false;
+
+/* Queue of not-yet-started notes. div + tick count are PRECOMPUTED on the
+   engine thread (SDL_DOSPcSpkBeep) so the ISR does ZERO divide; div==0 == a
+   timed REST (speaker silent for the duration). Monotonic int cursors, mutated
+   under DOS_DisableInterrupts vs the IRQ-0 consumer. DPMI-locked at Start. */
+static volatile struct { uint16_t div; uint16_t ticks; } s_beep_ring[PCSPK_NOTE_RING];
+static volatile int s_beep_wr = 0;
+static volatile int s_beep_rd = 0;
+
+/* Start a note NOW: program ch2 mode-3 square wave + route the speaker (or, for
+   a rest, gate the speaker off), then arm the countdown. outportb-only, no
+   divide -- called from BOTH the engine thread (under cli, in SDL_DOSPcSpkBeep)
+   and the IRQ-0 ISR (on note advance). DPMI-locked at Start. */
+static void BeepStartNote(uint16_t div, uint16_t ticks)
+{
+    if (div == 0u) {
+        /* timed REST: speaker + ch2 gate off, but keep the countdown running. */
+        outportb(0x61, (Uint8)(inportb(0x61) & ~0x03));
+    } else {
+        /* ch2: control 0x43 = 0xB6 (ch2, lobyte+hibyte, MODE 3 square wave,
+           binary), divisor to 0x42, then speaker on (0x61 bit0 = ch2 gate,
+           bit1 = speaker data). */
+        outportb(0x43, 0xB6);
+        outportb(0x42, (Uint8)(div & 0xFF));
+        outportb(0x42, (Uint8)((div >> 8) & 0xFF));
+        outportb(0x61, (Uint8)(inportb(0x61) | 0x03));
+    }
+    s_beep_ticks   = ticks ? ticks : 1u;
+    s_beep_playing = true;
+}
+static void BeepStartNote_End(void) {}
+
 /* Chain to the original BIOS INT 8 (it issues its own EOI). Simulate the
    interrupt entry: push flags, far-call the saved protected-mode vector; the
    handler's IRET pops EIP/CS/EFLAGS, balancing the CALL's CS/EIP + our pushfl.
@@ -1315,6 +1376,58 @@ static void OplPitISR(void)
 }
 static void OplPitISR_End(void) {}
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0118): PC-speaker-capable IRQ-0 ISR. Installed (instead
+   of the unchanged OplPitISR) ONLY when the PC-speaker SFX killswitch is on
+   (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PCSPK_SFX != "0", the default on the AdLib path). Same
+   clock advance + music tick + BIOS-INT8 chain as OplPitISR, plus: when a
+   square-wave note is sounding, count it down and -- on expiry -- advance to
+   the next queued note (or silence the speaker + go idle). outportb-only, no
+   divide (the note ring holds precomputed divisors). DPMI-locked. */
+static void OplPitBeepISR(void)
+{
+    /* 1. advance the monotonic clock (identical to OplPitISR). */
+    s_us_frac += s_us_per_tick;
+    while (s_us_frac >= 1000u) {
+        s_us_frac -= 1000u;
+        s_now_ms++;
+    }
+
+    /* 2. drive the music (the engine's ISR-safe MidiScheduler::tick_isr). */
+    if (s_pump_tick_cb) {
+        s_pump_tick_cb(s_now_ms);
+    }
+
+    /* 3. SDL/0118: PC-speaker note duration + monophonic sequencing. When the
+       current note's countdown hits zero, pop the next queued note (mode-3
+       square wave via BeepStartNote) or, if the ring is empty, gate the speaker
+       off and go idle. Nothing here runs while idle (s_beep_playing == false),
+       so an idle beep-ISR is one bool test heavier than OplPitISR. */
+    if (s_beep_playing) {
+        if (--s_beep_ticks == 0u) {
+            if (s_beep_rd != s_beep_wr) {
+                const int i = s_beep_rd & PCSPK_NOTE_MASK;
+                const uint16_t d = s_beep_ring[i].div;
+                const uint16_t t = s_beep_ring[i].ticks;
+                s_beep_rd++;
+                BeepStartNote(d, t);
+            } else {
+                outportb(0x61, (Uint8)(inportb(0x61) & ~0x03)); /* speaker + gate off */
+                s_beep_playing = false;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    /* 4. preserve the BIOS 18.2065 Hz tick (identical to OplPitISR). */
+    s_bios_accum += s_pit_div;
+    if (s_bios_accum >= 65536u) {
+        s_bios_accum -= 65536u;
+        OplPitChainOld();      /* original BIOS INT 8 runs + EOIs */
+    } else {
+        DOS_EndOfInterrupt(0); /* master-PIC EOI (IRQ-0) */
+    }
+}
+static void OplPitBeepISR_End(void) {}
+
 bool SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpStart(int hz)
 {
     if (s_opl_pump_active) {
@@ -1351,17 +1464,48 @@ bool SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpStart(int hz)
        (SDL_DOSMidiTickRegister) BEFORE Start, mirroring the SB init order. */
     s_pump_tick_cb = SDL_DOSMidiTickGetRegistered();
 
-    /* Install IRQ-0 via the REPLACE variant: an IRET wrapper enters OplPitISR
+    /* SDL/0118: resolve the PC-speaker SFX killswitch (strict-"0", DEFAULT ON;
+       pump Start only runs on the no-SB AdLib path, so this is inherently
+       AdLib-scoped). When "0", install the unchanged SDL/0110 music-only ISR
+       below -- byte-identical to v1.5.0, no ch2/0x61 touch. Also cache the ch0
+       fire rate (for ms->tick conversion) + snapshot port 0x61 for restore. */
+    {
+        const char *e = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PCSPK_SFX");
+        s_pcspk_sfx_enabled = !(e && e[0] == '0' && e[1] == '\0');
+    }
+    s_pcspk_fire_hz = (uint32_t)(DOS_PIT_INPUT_HZ / (s_pit_div ? s_pit_div : 1u));
+    if (s_pcspk_fire_hz == 0u) {
+        s_pcspk_fire_hz = 1u;
+    }
+    if (s_pcspk_sfx_enabled) {
+        s_beep_wr = s_beep_rd = 0;
+        s_beep_ticks = 0;
+        s_beep_playing = false;
+        s_pcspk_saved_61 = (Uint8)inportb(0x61);
+    }
+
+    /* Install IRQ-0 via the REPLACE variant: an IRET wrapper enters the handler
        as the terminal handler, so we own the EOI + the manual every-Nth chain
        (the chaining variant would run the old handler every fire == BIOS clock
-       ~6.6x fast at 120 Hz). */
-    DOS_HookInterruptReplace(0, OplPitISR, &s_opl_pit_hook);
+       ~6.6x fast at 120 Hz). SDL/0118: install the PC-speaker-capable ISR when
+       the killswitch is on, else the unchanged SDL/0110 music-only ISR (so the
+       flag-off path is byte-identical to v1.5.0). */
+    DOS_HookInterruptReplace(0, s_pcspk_sfx_enabled ? OplPitBeepISR : OplPitISR,
+                             &s_opl_pit_hook);
     s_old_int8_vec.off = (uint32_t)s_opl_pit_hook.original_irq_handler_seginfo.pm_offset;
     s_old_int8_vec.sel = (uint16_t)s_opl_pit_hook.original_irq_handler_seginfo.pm_selector;
 
-    /* DPMI-lock the ISR + chain helper + all ISR-touched data BEFORE arming
-       the fast PIT rate so no page-fault can occur in interrupt context. */
-    DOS_LockCode(OplPitISR, OplPitISR_End);
+    /* DPMI-lock the installed ISR + chain helper + all ISR-touched data BEFORE
+       arming the fast PIT rate so no page-fault can occur in interrupt context.
+       SDL/0118: lock the PC-speaker-capable ISR + BeepStartNote helper when the
+       killswitch is on (the ISR calls BeepStartNote on note advance); else the
+       unchanged music-only ISR. */
+    if (s_pcspk_sfx_enabled) {
+        DOS_LockCode(OplPitBeepISR, OplPitBeepISR_End);
+        DOS_LockCode(BeepStartNote, BeepStartNote_End);
+    } else {
+        DOS_LockCode(OplPitISR, OplPitISR_End);
+    }
     DOS_LockCode(OplPitChainOld, OplPitChainOld_End);
     DOS_LockVariable(s_pit_div);
     DOS_LockVariable(s_us_per_tick);
@@ -1371,6 +1515,15 @@ bool SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpStart(int hz)
     DOS_LockVariable(s_pump_tick_cb);
     DOS_LockVariable(s_old_int8_vec);
     DOS_LockVariable(s_opl_pump_active);
+    if (s_pcspk_sfx_enabled) {
+        /* SDL/0118: lock the note ring + all PC-speaker ISR-touched state. */
+        DOS_LockVariable(s_beep_ring);
+        DOS_LockVariable(s_beep_wr);
+        DOS_LockVariable(s_beep_rd);
+        DOS_LockVariable(s_beep_ticks);
+        DOS_LockVariable(s_beep_playing);
+        DOS_LockVariable(s_pcspk_fire_hz);
+    }
 
     /* Program PIT ch0: control 0x43 = 0x36 (ch0, lobyte+hibyte, mode 3,
        binary), then divisor low+high to 0x40. */
@@ -1388,6 +1541,11 @@ bool SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpStart(int hz)
                      (unsigned)(65536u / div),
                      s_pump_tick_cb ? "registered"
                                     : "NULL(no MidiScheduler tick registered!)");
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0118 [pcspk] square-wave SFX %s (PIT ch2 mode-3; "
+                     "ch0 pump %u Hz gates note duration; ring depth %d; killswitch "
+                     "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PCSPK_SFX=0 -> v1.5.0 music-only byte-identical)",
+                     s_pcspk_sfx_enabled ? "ENABLED" : "disabled (killswitch=0)",
+                     (unsigned)s_pcspk_fire_hz, PCSPK_NOTE_RING);
     return true;
 }
 
@@ -1402,6 +1560,21 @@ void SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpStop(void)
     outportb(0x43, 0x36);
     outportb(0x40, 0x00);
     outportb(0x40, 0x00);
+    if (s_pcspk_sfx_enabled) {
+        /* SDL/0118: tear down the PC speaker -- silence + restore ch2 to a
+           benign mode-3 state + port 0x61 to its pre-pump value. A left-on
+           square wave is a stuck tone, the same quit-path hazard class as the
+           PIT ch0 restore. This runs on normal Stop AND the engine's atexit
+           Stop (the single teardown path the AdLib pump wires), so ch2/0x61 are
+           always restored on exit. */
+        outportb(0x43, 0xB6);
+        outportb(0x42, 0x00);
+        outportb(0x42, 0x00);
+        outportb(0x61, s_pcspk_saved_61);
+        s_beep_playing = false;
+        s_beep_ticks = 0;
+        s_beep_wr = s_beep_rd = 0;
+    }
     s_opl_pump_active = false;
     DOS_EnableInterrupts();
 
@@ -1410,7 +1583,9 @@ void SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpStop(void)
     DOS_UnhookInterrupt(&s_opl_pit_hook, false);
 
     doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0110 OPL timer pump STOPPED (PIT ch0 restored "
-                     "to 18.2065 Hz; IRQ-0 unhooked; timer left unmasked)");
+                     "to 18.2065 Hz; IRQ-0 unhooked; timer left unmasked)%s",
+                     s_pcspk_sfx_enabled ? "; SDL/0118 PC-speaker restored (ch2+0x61)"
+                                         : "");
 }
 
 bool SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpActive(void)
@@ -1427,6 +1602,76 @@ bool SDL_DOSMidiIsrAnyActive(void)
     return SDL_DOSMidiIsrTickActive() || SDL_DOSOplTimerPumpActive();
 }
 
+/* ========================================================================
+ * DOSKUTSU patch (SDL/0118): PC-speaker square-wave SFX engine-facing API.
+ * The engine (nx-engine) maps Pixtone SFX IDs to (freq,duration) descriptors
+ * and calls SDL_DOSPcSpkBeep at its SFX trigger point. Contract:
+ * include/SDL3/SDL_dosopltimer.h.
+ * ======================================================================== */
+
+bool SDL_DOSPcSpkSfxEnabled(void)
+{
+    return s_pcspk_sfx_enabled;
+}
+
+void SDL_DOSPcSpkBeep(Uint16 freq_hz, Uint16 duration_ms, int flush)
+{
+    /* Safe no-op unless PC-speaker SFX is enabled (SDL-resolved at Start) AND
+       the ch0 pump is running -- so a stray call on a non-AdLib / killswitch-off
+       build never bangs ch2/0x61. A cached-bool read, NOT a per-call hint
+       lookup (the engine also gates its mapping on SDL_DOSPcSpkSfxEnabled()). */
+    if (!s_pcspk_sfx_enabled || !s_opl_pump_active) {
+        return;
+    }
+
+    /* Precompute the ch2 divisor + duration-in-fires HERE (engine thread) so the
+       IRQ-0 ISR does ZERO divide. freq_hz == 0 => a timed REST (div 0). */
+    uint16_t div;
+    if (freq_hz == 0) {
+        div = 0;
+    } else {
+        uint32_t f = freq_hz;
+        if (f < PCSPK_FREQ_MIN) f = PCSPK_FREQ_MIN;
+        if (f > PCSPK_FREQ_MAX) f = PCSPK_FREQ_MAX;
+        uint32_t d = DOS_PIT_INPUT_HZ / f;
+        if (d < 1u)     d = 1u;
+        if (d > 65535u) d = 65535u;
+        div = (uint16_t)d;
+    }
+    uint32_t dur = duration_ms ? (uint32_t)duration_ms : 1u;
+    if (dur > PCSPK_DUR_MAX) dur = PCSPK_DUR_MAX;
+    uint32_t ticks = (dur * s_pcspk_fire_hz + 999u) / 1000u; /* round up */
+    if (ticks < 1u)     ticks = 1u;
+    if (ticks > 65535u) ticks = 65535u;
+
+    /* Mutate the ring + note state under a brief interrupt-disable vs the IRQ-0
